From bc1df029921619593a05706339b0ef1ff5a9620d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: palazik <gochmyradov0@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 00:58:35 +0500
Subject: [PATCH] dodge: local TLB flush when leaving the bootstrap tables

Found by KSN2redawew/ios-giuliac (commit 5b5b104c), which patches the
two instructions in the built kernel.

arm_vm_init switches TTBR0 to invalid_ttep and then calls
flush_mmu_tlb(), which is "tlbi vmalle1is; dsb ish": a broadcast
invalidate that waits for every core in the inner shareable domain to
complete it. With the seven secondaries dormant in the DSU that can
never complete, and the result is a silent hang with no fault to report -
the one failure mode patch 0028's exception vectors cannot catch, since
nothing is actually faulting.

Nothing else is running at this point, xnu has not started the
secondaries yet, so a local invalidate is sufficient. xnu already has
exactly that pair as flush_core_tlb(), so this needs no new code.

Our own shim makes this more likely, not less: the granule probe now
starts all seven secondaries and powers them back off, so they are
dormant by the time xnu gets here.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 osfmk/arm64/arm_vm_init.c | 17 +++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 17 insertions(+)

diff --git a/osfmk/arm64/arm_vm_init.c b/osfmk/arm64/arm_vm_init.c
index 32499bd..827bcd8 100644
--- a/osfmk/arm64/arm_vm_init.c
+++ b/osfmk/arm64/arm_vm_init.c
@@ -2162,7 +2162,24 @@ arm_vm_init(uint64_t memory_size, boot_args * args)
 	dodge_early_disable();
 	set_mmu_ttb(invalid_ttep & TTBR_BADDR_MASK);
 
+#if defined(ARM64_BOARD_CONFIG_DODGE)
+	/*
+	 * Local flush, not the broadcast one. flush_mmu_tlb() is
+	 * "tlbi vmalle1is; dsb ish", which asks every core in the inner
+	 * shareable domain to complete the invalidate; with the seven
+	 * secondaries dormant in the DSU that can simply never complete, and
+	 * the result is a silent hang here with no fault to report. Nothing
+	 * else is running yet - xnu has not started the secondaries - so the
+	 * local invalidate is all this needs.
+	 *
+	 * Found by KSN2redawew/ios-giuliac (commit 5b5b104c), which patches
+	 * these two instructions in the built kernel; flush_core_tlb() is the
+	 * same pair, and xnu already provides it.
+	 */
+	flush_core_tlb();
+#else
 	flush_mmu_tlb();
+#endif
 	kva_active = TRUE;
 	// global table pointers may need to be different due to physical aperture remapping
 	cpu_tte = (tt_entry_t*)(phystokv(cpu_ttep));
